cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Portcullis: a static security analyzer for CI/CD pipeline definitions"
message: "If you use Portcullis in your research or tooling, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Portcullis contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/mk12002/Portcullis"
url: "https://github.com/mk12002/Portcullis"
abstract: >-
  Portcullis is a static, offline security analyzer for CI/CD pipeline
  definitions across GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, and Jenkins. It normalizes each
  platform into a shared model and applies platform-agnostic detection rules for
  dangerous triggers (pwn-requests), expression injection, action/image pinning,
  token permissions, secret exposure, and step integrity. Its distinguishing
  feature is trigger-context escalation: findings inside jobs reachable from an
  untrusted trigger are ranked more severe, reserving the merge-blocking priority
  for attacker-reachable criticals.
keywords:
  - security
  - ci-cd
  - github-actions
  - gitlab-ci
  - jenkins
  - static-analysis
  - supply-chain-security
  - sarif
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-07-19"
